From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: do not force XFI pause in pcs_post_config

airoha_pcs_post_config() unconditionally sets XFI TX/RX flow control
after airoha_pcs_config() has already programmed those bits from
permit_pause_to_mac. That makes XFI pause sticky on the AN7581 Ethernet
PCS used by GDM4 (W1700K lan2, USXGMII to RTL8261): even experiments
that clear the bits in pcs_config lose, and the netdev still comes up
with "flow control rx/tx".

Match the net-next airoha PCS series and leave frag/IPG setup alone in
pcs_post_config so pcs_config owns the FC enables.

On the AN7581 Ethernet PCS in USXGMII mode, keep XFI MAC pause off even
when phylink permits it. Pause on this hop stalls GDM4 transmit under
load and shows up as multi-tens-of-ms loaded latency versus the internal
GSW path (lan3). airoha_eth does not expose ethtool pause ops, so the PCS
is the only practical gate. PON PCS / wan are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c	2026-09-29 10:01:57.398480211 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c	2026-09-29 10:01:57.415938827 +0200
@@ -696,6 +696,14 @@
 				AIROHA_PCS_HSGMII_AN_SGMII_RESET_PHY);
 	}
 
+	/* XFI pause between eth PCS and the external 10G PHY stalls GDM4 TX
+	 * under load. Keep it off for AN7581 eth USXGMII; copper-side pause
+	 * remains a PHY/link-partner concern.
+	 */
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII &&
+	    device_is_compatible(priv->dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth"))
+		permit_pause_to_mac = false;
+
 	/* Configure Flow Control on XFI */
 	regmap_update_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
 			   AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN | AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN,
@@ -959,12 +967,6 @@
 			   AIROHA_PCS_XFI_IPG_NUM,
 			   FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_PCS_XFI_IPG_NUM, 10));
 
-	/* Enable TX/RX flow control */
-	regmap_set_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
-			AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN);
-	regmap_set_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
-			AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
